        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e0bc55dc4ea84bdbb474c97a9cefd3b6",
      "statement": "The core kit exports payments functions (getPlans, getSubscription, createCheckoutSession, openBillingPortal, getLicenses, grantLicense, revokeLicense, waitForSubscription), e-commerce functions (getCatalog, createOrder, getOrder, waitForOrder, readOrderRef, clearOrderRef), cart functions (addToCart, setCartQuantity, removeFromCart, cartTotals, toOrderItems, loadCart, saveCart, clearStoredCart), and price formatting (formatPrice).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/kit/src/index.ts#L10-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aac4ea6a06fb2adaaae87340eb2d9745f9ccf5071eda715ffc77447b2c21f25d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a58cd7b757ee4fa3a5f740d9f228a24d",
      "statement": "The payments subsystem is opt-in: setting payments: true in AuthConfig causes adapters to load the team's subscription on checkSession, login, and switchTeam, and expose subscription-related reactive state. When false or absent, no call to /stripe/* is ever made.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/kit/src/types.ts#L82-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea3adce503d00c28c68ab3f0ac350755ede895d80c0d13df0f3a60c75d6311e8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_26338d8fa5414771b69724da89347590",
      "statement": "Subscription state is resolved server-side from the database on every request (via SubscriptionVarResolver), not from the JWT. An upgrade is effective immediately with no re-login and no renewToken call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/kit/src/payments.ts#L5-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:962eca90cb942c43ad576a8c123f01f6dbc178435aa4438d0a410873d5aeed90:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_52fd3fe6f7be4b61a6ada5816d8c17f1",
      "statement": "The redirect back from Stripe Checkout races the webhook — a success page that calls getSubscription immediately may read the old plan. waitForSubscription and waitForOrder poll with a predicate until the condition is met, with the first check running immediately before any delay.",
