    {
      "id": "claim_df8ca19135774fe09841798e1f0a4da6",
      "statement": "The @ulabase/cli package provides the ulabase binary (with ula alias) with three commands: login (store a PAT), logout (forget the stored token), and setup (bring a service to the state a setup file describes). Every step is check-then-apply, so running it against an already-configured service writes nothing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/cli.ts#L119-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:502d97c3d3836f8cf7c8e0c6a56b8b757f98b55eb6c530c0d22bbb8a23ca95bb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/cli.ts#L58-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9800dcfbfedcbc41b3d04473b89ca0824eed541eec1427792108174f354a9b2b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_baa6cce2f4d74e0f959cdde918561e1e",
      "statement": "A CLI setup is declared with defineSetup (name + ordered steps) and each step with step (name + check + apply). The runner executes steps sequentially; a failure halts the rest. A dry run runs every check and applies nothing. After an apply, the runner re-checks with exponential backoff up to 15 seconds to handle admin-node/service-node cache lag.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/setup.ts#L108-L246",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06581a6826f7a04f4cf50d4aeac5365f7c77a2f509cc9ec696fe4c5178320589:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8be778fe48b34cc6abfac2cea151d77c",
      "statement": "fromEnv creates a typed string marker that stands for an environment variable name without holding its value. The value is resolved at apply time by the admin client when serializing the request body. A dry run never resolves one (no apply runs). toJSON throws to prevent unresolved markers from reaching the server as objects.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/env.ts#L1-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d0667c06ec2d6bb94ef5c97b3ce8149225dbf5900e69ab7ca7c237e2413bf6d6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_85feae8736624c7f8084401de6c3c578",
      "statement": "CLI credentials are personal access tokens (PATs) starting with 'ula_live_', carrying the 'cli' role. They are stored 0600 under ~/.config/ulabase by ulabase login, or set via ULABASE_TOKEN env var in pipelines. The env var always wins over a stored session. A credential is never accepted as a flag (to avoid shell history exposure).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/cli.ts#L101-L112",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42baf8cb963683d327ee3a3ac2b79c64a9e7b447e5d5059b1ef06c78a1056f91:"
